Show a boot or vendor_boot image's header, and with -o write its kernel, ramdisk, dtb, ...

Usage: android-doctor unpack [OPTIONS] <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  

Options:
      --no-color         Never emit colour, even on a terminal (also honours the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>  Write the sections (kernel, ramdisk, second, dtb, ...) into this directory
      --json             Print the header as JSON
      --force            Replace existing files instead of refusing
  -h, --help             Print help
